# Pens ported from the old VanGuard build.
ent-PenAtmos = blue atmospheric pen
    .desc = A not too sophisticated pen in your department's colours. You stick to it because it matches your palette.
ent-PenBooze = brown booze pen
    .desc = A pen in the colours of a whiskey bottle. Might just have a hidden vial inside, you'll never know.
ent-PenCargo = orange cargo pen
    .desc = A cheap writing tool made of slightly abrasive cardboard, easy to hold in sweaty hands. Your head probably buys these in bulk.
ent-PenChaplain = black chaplain's pen
    .desc = A black and white pen made of glossy plastic and stainless steel. Looks great and is not too expensive.
ent-PenChemist = orange chemist's pen
    .desc = A solid piece of cheap white plastic with orange details. Why do you even need it, all your experiments are practical anyway.
ent-PenEngineering = yellow engineering pen
    .desc = A pen with an old-style feel: yellowed plastic and details of an old fax printer make your paperwork a little more comfortable.
ent-PenGreen = green pen
    .desc = A light-green version of your standard writing equipment.
ent-PenHearts = pink hearts pen
    .desc = A bright pink pen thoroughly decorated with hearts. They say you should put your heart into writing.
ent-PenHydroponics = green hydroponics pen
    .desc = Toxic green and blue plastic. This paint is now stuck to your skin forever. Hopefully your plants are treated better than that.
ent-PenJanitor = purple janitorial pen
    .desc = Standard-issue grey and purple NanoTrasen pen. Actually worth more than it seems.
ent-PenLightBlue = light-blue medical pen
    .desc = A light-blue version of your standard writing equipment. Wait, isn't it straight from medbay?
ent-PenMedical1 = blue medical pen
    .desc = Your normal blue pen, just what you'd expect from a medical office. Easy to use and sanitize too.
ent-PenMedical2 = cheap blue medical pen
    .desc = Your normal blue pen. Hold on, is it a cheaper version? Still just as easy to sanitize.
ent-PenCamouflage = green camouflage pen
    .desc = A military-design office writing tool. As useful for special operations as it is for a fishing vacation.
ent-PenMime = gray mime pen
    .desc = Sometimes silence is worth more than a handful of words. For any other occasion this pen is stocked with twice the ink.
ent-PenPink = pink pen
    .desc = They say human hearts are pink. Are other species this way too? With this pen you will surely linger in all the hearts.
ent-PenPurple = purple magic pen
    .desc = All the magic is actually the presentation. Use that to your advantage and win the audience with your mystique.
ent-PenRainbow = purple rainbow fountain pen
    .desc = A cheerful fountain pen prone to joyful splashes of ink at the cost of your documents. No, the ink is plain, why'd you ask?
ent-PenMedia = blue media pen
    .desc = A pen of a formal design powered by several enhancements that make interviewing in the wildest places a lot easier.
ent-PenYellow = yellow pen
    .desc = A light-yellow version of your standard writing equipment.
ent-PenViolet = purple violet pen
    .desc = A violet version of your standard writing equipment.
ent-PenStarry = purple starry pen
    .desc = Deep violet shades look just like the view outside. Scattered white dots represent the wildest opportunities for you. Go take them all!
ent-PenScienceFountain = light-blue science fountain pen
    .desc = A piece of scientific progress, its main contribution being writing off reports. Uses an advanced ink supply system for more reliable strokes.
ent-PenScienceOverpriced = blue overpriced science pen
    .desc = A pen you probably spent too much on. It isn't any different from the standard-issue one, so what's wrong with the price? At least the build quality is worth it.
ent-PenScience = blue science pen
    .desc = A medium-quality pen of the science department. You have inspected all you could and the final verdict: the pen is boring. Just as much as your paperwork.
ent-PenBrigmedic = red brigmedic pen
    .desc = An overly red pen with a white cross sticker plastered on top. Shows how little the corpos care about qualified on-the-spot medicine.
ent-PenSecurityBlack = black security pen
    .desc = A thoroughly decorated black and red security pen. Not too good, not too shabby, mediocre.
ent-PenSecurityRed = red security pen
    .desc = A simplistic red plastic pen. Looks great and is not overly complicated, just right for all the hardheads out there.
ent-PenSecurityFountain = red security fountain pen
    .desc = Somehow even less reliable than the usual security pen, you just learned to live with it. Even if it doesn't work at times.
ent-PenSecurityFountainMetallic = red metallic security fountain pen
    .desc = The head of security's preferred writing tool. Made of pure stainless steel with some sickly red elements. It will keep working even a century later.
ent-BlackFountainPen = black fountain pen
    .desc = A stylish black fountain pen for signing off the most devilish orders.
ent-PenMedicalCMO = light-blue medical fountain pen
    .desc = The chief medical officer's fountain pen: elegance and cleanliness. It makes it even easier to encrypt your medical records in unreadable handwriting.
ent-PenEngineeringCE = yellow engineer fountain pen
    .desc = The chief engineer's fountain pen looks like an electrician's nightmare. A pleasant yellow colour and winding in the style of ancient microcircuits warm the soul of those who like to sit in the office.
ent-PenCargo1QM = gold cargo fountain pen
    .desc = The quartermaster's fountain pen, it seems to be gilded. Your employees shouldn't know where you got it from.
